                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2762622,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "And because it was already so busy, prospectors began to look for other minerals, and by the end of the nineteenth century, lead, copper, manganese, and arsenic were added to the cargoes leaving Manham.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 144.855,
                  "from": 131.89499,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 1"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2762657,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "In the early days, the ores had been smelted or processed in the same area they were mined.",
